  "question": {
    "text": "A circle with centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> intersects the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. If the tangents at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "11",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A Circle having the centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>So, the equation of circle will be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now, it is&nbsp;given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;passes through two points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> on circle and&nbsp;tangents are drawn at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;intersect at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;will be chord of contact.</p><p>Now equation of chord of contact will be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now comparing above equation with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now on solving above relation&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p>"
  }
